.TH EDUKA-TET 1 "2026-10-12" "0.3.0" "Edukasaun OS"
.SH NAME
eduka-tet \- Tetun locale and community language resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eduka-tet
status|doctor|demo|resources|glossary [query]|normalize|run -- command
.br
.B eduka-tet
enable --user [--desktop NAME] [--accounts-service]
.br
.B eduka-tet
disable --user
.br
.B sudo eduka-tet
compile-locale
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides an INL-oriented community language draft. No INL certification is
claimed. Installation compiles tet_TL.UTF-8 against the target libc. Applications
need matching catalogs; not every Debian application is translated.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable --user
Save reversible login/Xsession and systemd user environment settings.
Plasma uses its native language keys; GNOME can use AccountsService.
Run without sudo, then log out and log in again.
.TP
.B disable --user
Restore previous managed settings; preserve unrelated user edits; log in again.
.TP
.B doctor
Show locale availability, desktop detection and partial catalog coverage.
.TP
.B run -- command
Execute a program in a temporary Tetun environment.
.TP
.B normalize
Read standard input and emit NFC text with ASCII apostrophes.
.TP
.B compile-locale
Compile package-owned locale data; requires root.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/eduka-language-pack-tet
.br
/usr/share/locale/tet/LC_MESSAGES/
.br
/usr/share/i18n/locales/tet_TL
.br
/usr/lib/locale/tet_TL.utf8
.SH SEE ALSO
locale(1), localedef(1), update-locale(8)
